    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today leans heavily on high-leverage matchups to maximize efficiency, with **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) headlining the card as our must-start anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a rare intersection of a favorable SP skill matchup against Peralta and, crucially, a slow-delivery pitcher that boosts his SB upside\u2014the scarcest commodity in our build. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** is primed for a breakout performance, facing the league\u2019s most generous matchup in Bradford (5.29 xERA). His score is buoyed by an excellent 10% park factor and the SP skill differential, making him our most efficient play for aggregate production today.\n\nWhile the top of the order carries the day, we are leveraging favorable platoon splits for **Jackson Merrill** (69.56), whose dynamic platoon advantage (13%) and spot in the #5 hole make him a stronger start than the baseline suggests. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Kyle Tucker** (51.47); despite his pedigree, the matchup against Henderson (2.84 xERA) suppresses his ceiling, relegating him to a utility role to preserve game caps. Our most difficult decision involved **Coby Mayo** (43.08), who fell just shy of our starting threshold. While the slow delivery of Peralta tempted a start, **Coby Mayo** was ultimately sidelined due to a lower projected efficiency relative to the rest of the infield and his unfavorable position at #8 in the lineup.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the heavy slate of right-handed pitchers we face today. Matchups against elite arms like Henderson and Cease have forced us to bench players like **Luis Lara** (39.29), whose efficiency dipped below our 40.0 floor due to a high-difficulty matchup against Skubal. Additionally, while **Heliot Ramos** and **Luis Robert Jr.** carry the physical tools to swing a matchup, their scores are dampened by dynamic platoon regression. We will monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains on the IL, as we look to navigate these SP-heavy pairings to keep our 5x5 categories competitive.",
